You probably prayed too soon, you have to be at <= 1/7 of your maximum
hp (or less than 6 hp, whichever is higher) to be healed.

> Now I stand face to face with a Woodland-Elf at 1 HP and don't know
> what to do. I am slightly burdened which makes matters worse I guess.

Being burdened is a major no-no. Having 1 less move every 3 turns
means, in effect, that you do 25% less damage than you would in normal
melee--the elves are getting free attacks where they hurt you, but you
can't hurt them.  Worse, it can turn a lot of curable problems (like
cockatrice stoning, where all you have to do is take a bite of that
lizard you're carrying around, or pray if you lack a lizard) into
instant unavoidable deaths.

And it means that you can't capitalize on speed, so a monster that you
could do hit-run-run-hit-run-run etc and kill it without it ever
having a chance to attack suddenly becomes a threat.  You get less
missile attacks before they close with you.

Also, you hunger faster.

It's just nasty.  Don't do it.

