If you recognized the situation very early on, it might be worth
trying to poly them into something Elbereth-respecting, though I
probably wouldn't try that.  In your current situation it's a very low
percentage; better off polying yourself, and getting full hp after you
revert (at which point you can polyself again if you still need to to
get out of trouble).

> If these options are not as advisable as I think they are ... what
> would you suggest ?

I'd suggest that your mistakes are probably made earlier in the game,
which won't help now (/poly seems best from what you've listed), but
in the future you might want to consider:

Don't be burdened.  What's the choke point where you stood?  I stand
diagonally from the door to limit ranged attacks, though standing
directly in front of it means you can only be adjacent to 2 monsters.
Keeping one of your pets ahead of you means that you can be diagonal,
have the pet there to fight, and still only face 2 monsters--and when
the doorway's clear, it'll often go ahead and take things out while
you sit there in relative safety.

What's your AC and damage output?  What XL?  Are you being careful to
accumulate AC as fast as possible?  The fact that you're still in your
splint mail by Sokoban means you _might_ not be (usually you'll have
mithril by there, but not always--certainly you can hope to have found
some boots and maybe other armor upgrades, and probably bought the
first round of protection).

Especially if you're relatively weak for this stage of the game, you
should be sending pet(s) ahead of you into danger areas.  As a
spellcaster I'll ditch them a bit earlier, and once I get tougher I'll
do likewise, but until just before the mid-game they're incredibly
valuable.



